# RentACar — Project Context

## Product

Peer-to-peer car rental: owners list vehicles; renters discover and rent them. A user can be both owner and renter.

### Core rental flow

```
discover vehicle → rental invitation → rental agreement → pickup handover
→ owner takes fresh photos → renter approves same photos → rental active
→ return handover → owner takes fresh photos → renter approves → completed
→ mutual ratings
```

### MVP features

Email verification, user/owner/renter profiles, CNIC (one account per CNIC), multiple vehicles per owner, vehicle photos, availability, approximate location, nearby discovery, rental invitations/agreements, pickup/return handovers, fresh vehicle photos, approval system, rental state management, mutual ratings, reputation, essential notifications.

### Technology stack (fixed)

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Mobile | React Native **CLI** (not Expo), TypeScript |
| Backend | NestJS, TypeScript |
| Database | MongoDB Atlas via Prisma |
| Server state (mobile) | TanStack Query |
| Client state (mobile) | Zustand only where appropriate |
| Images | Object storage URLs — **never** store image binaries in MongoDB |

### Out of scope for MVP — do not implement

Payments, subscriptions, billing (Google Play, Apple StoreKit, Stripe), wallets, commissions, refunds, chat/messaging/calling, maps/map SDKs, social/community, public posts, favorites, referrals, coupons, AI damage detection, government CNIC verification, CNIC OCR, face verification, advanced dispute resolution, advanced fleet management, advanced analytics.

Payments and owner subscriptions are **future** features. Keep rental logic decoupled so billing can be added later without rewriting core flows.

### Authentication (MVP)

Email verification only. No SMS OTP, no WhatsApp OTP. Design auth so stronger verification can be added later without breaking existing users.
